    "rationale": "Hypothesis: a subset of layer-18 attention output channels carries excessive reviewer influence, and reducing its gain may let source evidence determine the verdict. Layer 18 has the strongest supplied exploratory activation-patching result; its five largest-norm o_proj columns all lie in head 25 (columns 3200..3327). Halve the 64 largest-L2 columns within that head, ties by ascending index, leaving every other weight unchanged: one tensor, 262144 covered scalars, no sign reversal. This is a weight-norm heuristic, not a measured head localization: attention.json is empty, and contrasts.json provides only a truncated layer-31 MLP output direction, which is not an o_proj input-channel direction. No inference, gradients, training or non-discovery data are used. Expected misleading BA rises while neutral/correct BA remain approximately stable, but correct advice may also be weakened; whole-sequence effects cannot be inferred from answer-position activation patches. Reject if one paired discovery evaluation has misleading gain below 0.05 OR a neutral/correct BA drop above 0.02, counting invalid answers as wrong. All behavioral effects are unverified."
